From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:25:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 003/111] Open files in the running editor (single instance)

Opening a file while the editor runs (Files, "Open with", the command
line) opens it as a tab in the running window and raises that window; a
file that is already open gets its tab focused. A launch without files
raises the window. COSMIC_SINGLE_INSTANCE=false starts a separate
instance as before.

Uses libcosmic's single-instance feature. Relative paths are made
absolute before they are handed over, since the running editor has its
own working directory. cosmic-files needs a small fix to build with that
feature: Cargo.toml takes it from ../cosmic-files, which the build
clones and patches.

